                    HEPU OS ADDITIONAL TERMS
              (pursuant to GPLv3 Section 7 "Additional Terms")

In addition to the terms of the GNU General Public License version 3,
the HEPU OS project imposes the following additional terms:

  1. KERNEL FINGERPRINT PRESERVATION
     The read-only kernel copyright fingerprint structure (HEPU_FINGERPRINT)
     compiled into the kernel binary MUST NOT be removed, modified, or
     bypassed. Any distributed version must retain the kernel source
     attribution in user-visible interfaces.

  2. TRADEMARK RESTRICTION
     The names "赫普OS", "HEPU OS", "HEPU Hyper Evolve OS", and the
     official HEPU OS logo are trademarks of the HEPU OS Project.
     Third-party derivative works MUST NOT use these trademarks without
     official authorization. Derivative works must use a distinct name
     and clearly state "based on HEPU OS open-source microkernel".

  3. SANDBOX INTEGRITY
     You may not remove or bypass the privacy sandbox, permission control
     mechanisms, or install invisible user-data collection modules into
     the system.

  4. SOURCE ATTRIBUTION
     Any OEM or vendor distributing a HEPU OS-based system must display
     kernel source attribution in at least three locations:
     (a) the "About Device" settings page,
     (b) the firmware download / documentation page,
     (c) the boot-time copyright notice.

These additional terms are enforced under GPLv3 Section 7.
If any of these terms is held unenforceable, the remaining terms remain
in full effect.

